<div class="page-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">BEHIND THE CLUB</p><h1>Made for movement.</h1><p class="page-intro">A straightforward way to keep a sports club organized.</p></div></div>
<div class="row g-4"><div class="col-lg-7 surface p-4 p-lg-5"><h2>One club, one place</h2><p>Clubhouse is an academic Sports Club Management System. It brings trainers, members, training sessions, and enrollment into a single responsive web application.</p><p>Create and update club records, explore the upcoming schedule, register members for training, and cancel enrollments. Session capacity and duplicate enrollment checks help keep the schedule accurate.</p><h3 class="mt-4">Project</h3><p class="mb-0">Developed as a university coursework project by Veselin Maslenkov, Faculty Number 450 IT remote.</p></div><div class="col-lg-5"><div class="surface p-4 h-100"><p class="eyebrow">UNDER THE HOOD</p><h2>A simple MVC foundation</h2><dl class="detail-list"><dt>Backend</dt><dd>C# · ASP.NET Core MVC · .NET 10</dd><dt>Database</dt><dd>SQLite through Entity Framework Core</dd><dt>Interface</dt><dd>Razor views · Bootstrap 5</dd><dt>Architecture</dt><dd>Models store club data, controllers handle requests, and views render the interface. A small service handles enrollment transactions.</dd></dl></div></div></div>
